# Parser Redesign — Lark Grammar + AST + Visitor Architecture

## The Big Idea

Replace our hand-written tokenizer + positional AST builder with a **formal grammar** (Lark EBNF) + **auto-generated parse tree** + **visitor/compiler** that emits safe MongoDB queries. Keep the **semantic resolver** for field/collection matching. Add **NLP libraries** for dates, synonyms, fuzzy matching.

```
User NL text
    ↓
Text Normalizer (spaCy lemma, synonym expand, dateparser, autocorrect)
    ↓
Lark Grammar Parser (EBNF rules → auto AST)
    ↓
AST (LogicalNode, ComparisonNode, AggNode, SortNode, ProjectionNode, LimitNode)
    ↓
MongoCompiler (visitor walks AST → safe MongoDB dict)
    ↓
Query Guards (whitelist operators, block $where, depth/size limits)
    ↓
{ query, explanation, confidence, warnings }
```

### Why Lark over hand-written
| | Hand-written (current) | Lark grammar (proposed) |
|---|---|---|
| Parentheses [(A and B) or C](file:///c:/Users/Prashant/Documents/NLMongo_Project/nl_to_mongo/backend/routes/chat.py#27-107) | ❌ Not supported | ✅ Grammar handles recursion |
| Operator precedence | ❌ Ad-hoc, bugs | ✅ Grammar rules define it |
| Adding new operators | Must edit 3 files | Add 1 grammar rule |
| Ambiguity | Silent wrong output | Lark Earley parser resolves it |
| Multi-word values | ❌ Broken | ✅ Quoted string in grammar |
| Maintainability | 900+ lines across 4 files | Grammar file + compiler |

