## Phase 2 — Benchmark Integration

### [NEW] [benchmarks/](file:///c:/Users/Prashant/Documents/NLMongo_Project/nl_to_mongo/benchmarks/)

Download and adapt:
- **DocSpider** `dev.json` (766 NL→MQL pairs) 
- **MongoDB mongosh** `benchmark.csv` (766 pairs across 8 DBs)
- **Custom evaluator** that feeds NL to our parser and compares output

---

## Phase 3 — Guards & Safety

- Whitelist allowed MongoDB operators
- Block: `$where`, `$function`, `$accumulator` (code injection risk)
- Max pipeline depth: 10 stages
- Max result limit: 50 documents
- Query timeout: 30 seconds

---

## Execution Order

| Step | What | Risk |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Install deps (lark, spacy, dateparser, rapidfuzz, nltk, inflect) | None |
| 2 | Write `nlquery.lark` grammar file | Low |
| 3 | Write `normalizer.py` (text preprocessor) | Low |
| 4 | Write `compiler.py` (AST → MongoDB visitor) | Medium |
| 5 | Update [parser_engine.py](file:///c:/Users/Prashant/Documents/NLMongo_Project/nl_to_mongo/parser/parser_engine.py) (new pipeline with old fallback) | Medium |
| 6 | Run 35-test regression | Checkpoint |
| 7 | Add new test cases (parentheses, either/or, multi-sort, typos) | Low |
| 8 | Download + integrate benchmarks | Low |
| 9 | Query guards + explanation output | Low |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Full Lark system — old parser modules will be replaced entirely.

